@page "/"

<PageTitle>Home</PageTitle>

<h1>Welcome to the team!</h1>

<p>Your .NET 10 development environment is up and running.</p>

<h2>Explore the application</h2>
<ul>
    <li><a href="counter">Counter</a>: try an interactive Blazor component.</li>
    <li><a href="weather">Weather</a>: load a five-day forecast from the API.</li>
    <li>Open the Aspire dashboard to inspect resources, logs, metrics, and traces.</li>
</ul>

<h2>What is running?</h2>
<p>
    Aspire starts this Blazor frontend, an ASP.NET Core API, and a Redis container.
    The frontend discovers the API by name. The API caches its forecast in Redis
    for five seconds. The forecast is randomly generated, so no external API key
    or cloud account is needed.
</p>
